---
const rows = [
  { k: "Deployment", v: "Runs inside your environment. <b>Compute on Assembly AWS</b>, customer data stays in your systems &mdash; or fully single-tenant managed in your VPC." },
  { k: "Identity & access", v: "SSO via Okta or Entra. SCIM provisioning. Role-scoped reviewer access on every HITL gate. No shared accounts." },
  { k: "Human-in-the-loop", v: "Every judgment call surfaces in a named reviewer's queue with SLA. <b>No silent autonomous decisioning, ever.</b>" },
  { k: "Audit lineage", v: "Every action traces back: source record, rule that fired, model call, reviewer who approved. The trail an examiner would ask for &mdash; already there." },
  { k: "Compliance posture", v: "SOC 2 Type II &middot; ISO 27001 (in progress) &middot; HIPAA &amp; GLBA-aligned data handling." },
  { k: "Model isolation", v: "Customer-isolated inference. <b>No training on your data.</b> Model audit log retained for the life of the engagement." },
];
---

<section class="gov" id="governance">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head">
      <div class="left">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Enterprise governance, by default</span>
        <h2>The plumbing your AI tooling <em>doesn't ship with</em>.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <p>
          This is the dimension on which AI coding tooling and in-house prototypes break down. In regulated environments &mdash; or any environment with an auditor &mdash; the governance posture is the product. We ship it on day one, not as a phase two.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gov-grid">
      <div class="gov-card">
        <h3>Built in, not bolted on</h3>
        <p class="sub">Six properties the buyer's security and compliance team will ask about. Each one is the thing an off-the-shelf AI tool leaves to you.</p>
        <div class="gov-rows">
          {
            rows.map(({ k, v }) => (
              <div class="r">
                <span class="k">{k}</span>
                <span class="v" set:html={v} />
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="gov-side">
        <div class="side-card lift">
          <span class="side-eyebrow">Pricing</span>
          <h4>Priced on the work we ship.</h4>
          <p>Usage-based on the unit of work the application does &mdash; not on seats, hours, or developer count. Annual commit available.</p>
          <a href="/pricing" class="side-link">
            See pricing <span class="arr">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="side-card alt">
          <span class="side-eyebrow">Deployment</span>
          <h4>Your environment, your sign-on.</h4>
          <p>Single-tenant in your VPC or managed on Assembly AWS. Customer data never leaves your systems.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .gov {
    padding: 120px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ink-100);
    background: #fff;
  }
  .s-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 80px;
    margin-bottom: 56px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 920px) { .s-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; } }
  .s-head .left .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 14px; display: block; }
  .s-head h2 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--color-indigo-600); }
  .s-head .right p { color: var(--color-ink-500); font-size: 18px; max-width: 680px; }

  .gov-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .gov-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .gov-card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: 36px;
  }
  .gov-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 26px;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .gov-card .sub {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .gov-rows { display: grid; }
  .gov-rows .r {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ink-100);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .gov-rows .r:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .gov-rows .r .k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .gov-rows .r .v {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .gov-rows .r .v :global(b) { color: var(--color-ink-950); font-weight: 600; }

  .gov-side {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .side-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--color-ink-50);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .side-card.alt {
    background: var(--color-ink-950);
    border-color: transparent;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .side-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
  }
  .side-card.alt .side-eyebrow { color: var(--color-lavender-300); }
  .side-card h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 19px;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--color-ink-950);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .side-card.alt h4 { color: #fff; }
  .side-card p {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .side-card.alt p { color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); }
  .side-link {
    margin-top: 8px;
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-indigo-600);
    text-decoration: none;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }
  .side-link:hover .arr { transform: translateX(3px); }
  .side-link .arr { transition: transform 0.2s; }
</style>
